// Reports what merging 2 to 10 git services of one environment into a single service with several processes would do, and whether it can start. The target keeps running and gains one process per other service (their start command, port, health check, limits and replicas); they share its one build, image, variables and release. `blocking` lists what prevents the start (`not_combinable`, `source_mismatch`, `server_mismatch`, `agent_too_old`, `source_has_volumes`, `already_has_processes`, `port_conflict`, `task_name_conflict`, `source_referenced`, ...); `variables.conflicts` lists the variables the services set to different values (the start needs a choice for each; secrets are compared by value and never shown); `domainMoves` and `taskMoves` are what moves to the target at the cutover. `fingerprint` binds a start to this plan. It changes nothing.
