//
// Without parameters the project must be empty: it fails with 409 `project_not_empty` while a service is left. With `cascade=true` the project goes with everything in it, irreversibly: its previews, every service of every environment with its volumes (the agents remove the containers and volumes), the status page components that show those services, the DNS records NebulaCtrl manages for their domains, the shared variables, the environments, then the project. `confirm` must equal the project's name (422 `confirm_mismatch`). Backups already written to backup destinations stay. See `GET /projects/{projectId}/deletion-plan` for the counts. MCP principals need an approval when the project has a production environment. A deployment in progress is refused with 409 `deployment_in_progress`, and read replicas of a database with 409 `project_has_replicas`.
