// CreateDumpRestoreWithBody Restore a database from a dump file
//
// Prepares a restore of a managed database from a file you upload: a `pg_dump` file (custom `-Fc`, tar `-Ft` or plain SQL, optionally gzipped), a `mysqldump`/`mariadb-dump` SQL file (optionally gzipped) or a `mongodump --archive` file. mode `new` (default) creates a sibling database and deploys it empty; mode `in_place` first takes a safety backup (needs `confirmSlug`) and then replaces this database's data. Poll the restore until its status is `awaiting_upload`, then send the file: `PUT /api/v1/dump-restores/{restoreId}/upload` with the file as the raw request body (`Content-Type: application/octet-stream`, `Content-Length` required, optional `?fileName=`). It answers 202 once the agent has the whole file (status `restoring`); poll `GET /dump-restores/{restoreId}` for `succeeded` or `failed`. The control plane stores nothing: the bytes stream through it to the agent. The format is detected from the file's first bytes (422 `unsupported_dump_format` when it does not fit the engine); 413 `file_too_large` above the limit (`maxUploadBytes`, default 5 GiB).
