// CheckStatusPageDNS Check the DNS of a status page's hostname
//
// The A and AAAA records the hostname needs (the control-plane server's public addresses) and whether the hostname resolves to them right now. The hostname is looked up at the zone's authoritative nameservers, so a name that exists is never reported missing because of a cached answer; answers are kept for 60 seconds, and `fresh=true` skips that cache. A page whose Cloudflare record is proxied is `ok` when the hostname resolves to Cloudflare's addresses (`proxied: true`), not `mismatch`. `cloudflareRecord` says Cloudflare's API confirmed the record exists: a `missing` hostname then only waits for DNS caches. 422 `no_hostname` while the page has no hostname.
