// Creates a new, non-production environment in the same project with a staged copy of every service of the source: configuration, variables, the environment's shared variables, volume definitions, links, repository links and canvas layout. Slugs are kept, so references such as `${{postgres.DATABASE_URL}}` point at the cloned siblings. Secrets are copied sealed and generated values are generated again. Databases are created new and empty: restore a dump into them. Volumes are new and empty. Domains are dropped (default) or cloned with a suffix; 409 `domain_conflict` when a suffixed hostname is taken. Route services and Compose stacks are skipped and listed. Nothing runs until the services are deployed. `dryRun` returns the plan and changes nothing.
