// CombineServicesWithBodyWithResponse Combine services into one
//
// Starts merging the services of a reviewed plan (202). The target is staged with one process per other service and variables chosen with `variableChoices`; the other services are not touched and keep serving. A deployment of the target then builds once and rolls every process, all or nothing. Only when it succeeded do the domains and scheduled tasks of the other services move to the target, in one step with one route table, and the other services are deleted (their volumes are kept). If the deployment fails nothing was deleted: the combine is `failed`, and can be retried or aborted. A stale `fingerprint` is 409 `plan_stale`; a missing variable choice 422 `variable_choice_required`. Deleting services needs approval for guarded clients in production.
