// SetServerUnrestrictedWithBodyWithResponse Make a server unrestricted, or restricted again
//
// By default Compose stacks and services run under safe allow-lists: no privileged mode, host network, host PID namespace, devices, GPUs, custom runtime, unconfined seccomp or AppArmor, NET_ADMIN or SYS_ADMIN, Docker socket or host bind mounts. An unrestricted server lifts them for everything on it, so anyone who can deploy there can take over the server. Instance admin only; enabling needs `confirm` to equal the server's name. Audited as `server.unrestricted.enable` or `.disable`. Disabling does not touch running containers: the next deploy, rollback or reconcile of a stack or service that needs the lifted rules fails until it is edited or moved.
