// CloneServiceWithBodyWithResponse Clone a service
//
// Creates a staged copy of a service in the same or another environment of the team; nothing runs until it is deployed. The clone gets the source's configuration (Docker options included), variables, volume definitions and, in the same environment, its outgoing links. Secrets are copied sealed and generated values are generated again. Volumes are new and empty (the data is not copied). A managed database is created new and empty with new credentials: restore a dump into it. Domains are dropped (default) or cloned with a suffix; 409 `domain_conflict` when a suffixed hostname is taken. Needs write access to the source and the target environment. Route services, Compose stacks and read replicas are not cloned (422 `not_applicable`). `dryRun` returns the plan and changes nothing; the response lists variable references that do not resolve in the target environment.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
