// PromoteDatabaseReplicaWithBodyWithResponse Promote a read replica to primary (manual)
//
// Called on the replica. Manual: NebulaCtrl does not detect failures or switch automatically. With `dryRun` the plan is returned (status 200): `switchover` while the old primary is reachable (it is frozen, stopped and fenced, the replica replays everything, no data is lost) or `forced` otherwise (it needs `acceptDataLoss`: what the replica had not received is lost). The old primary is fenced and never runs as a primary again; rebuild it as a replica or delete it. Variables that reference the old primary are rewritten as staged changes. Production environments need approval. Asynchronous: poll `replication.promotion`.
