// DeleteTeamWithResponse Delete a team with everything in it
//
// Owners only, signed in as a person. Requires `confirm=<slug>`. Starts a background job and answers 202 with the team: its `deletion` says where the job is. It deletes every project with its services, volumes and domains, removes the platform services, then every server (the agent of an online server empties its host and removes itself; an offline server is removed without touching its host and listed in `deletion.forgottenServers`), the status pages, the Cloudflare connection (the DNS records NebulaCtrl created are deleted unless `keepDnsRecords=true`), the tailnet integration with the devices and keys NebulaCtrl created, and finally the team. Backups already written to backup destinations stay there. If a step fails the team stays, `deletion.state` is `failed` with the reason, and deleting again retries. 409 `team_hosts_control_plane` when the team owns the server NebulaCtrl runs on, 409 `deletion_in_progress`. Denied to MCP agents.
